; Leg HN -- the rcvfil() stall pair -- receive into D:\ at 9600.
;
; BENCH take-file: there is no "set line" here.  ~/.kermrc names the adapter.
; CHECK THAT IT NAMES THE ONE THAT IS PLUGGED IN.
;
; Run HL immediately after this one.  ONE VARIABLE: the volume.
;
; SS16ba killed five candidates for the ~27 s F-packet stall and left one --
; something about the ROOT DIRECTORY ITSELF (capacity, deleted 0xE5 slots,
; entry fragmentation), with zchko() doing three DOS directory operations on
; it before a data byte moves.  Under MAME a clean 9600 receive is 46.1-46.6 s
; and 702-710 cps where A:\ gives 78.9 and 415.
;
; THIS IS THE ONE LEG IN THE SITTING THAT RUNS -d ON PURPOSE, and SS16aw
; permits it because the stall is a discrete 26-second event and not a
; throughput claim.  Expect deb=1.  DO NOT QUOTE A CPS FIGURE OFF EITHER LEG.
;
; The observable is the gap between the F packet and its ACK in the packet
; log, and three timeouts at 8, 16 and 24 s if it is there.
;
; READ IT WITH:
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <from STEPHN.OUT> s16bcHN.pkt
; Residual -11 clean, +28 with a startup timeout.
; cmp FIRST, then the counters.  A leg that is fast and wrong is the failure.

set speed 9600
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
log packets s16bcHN.pkt
send rcvhn.dat
statistics
